## §3 Generating Android-ready graphics **[core]**

> **CRITICAL:** For all Play Store asset design rules (colors, composition, video durations, ASO naming), you MUST strictly follow `play-store-assets-generation.mdc`. The guidelines below cover only the technical Android implementation (sizes, formats, tooling).

### Play Store asset spec

| Asset | Size | Format | Rules |
|-------|------|--------|-------|
| **App icon (listing)** | **512×512** | **32-bit PNG ONLY** | **CRITICAL: No JPEGs.** Must include alpha channel. Flat 2D graphic only (no device photos). **ASO Rule:** Icon must be hyper-literal and physically show the core mechanic (e.g., a 3x3 grid of 1s). Avoid purely abstract branding logos. Keep core art inside a **15% padding safe zone** to account for Google's automatic 30% squircle mask. |
| **Feature graphic** | **1024×500** | PNG/JPEG | Exact dimensions required (1023x500 will fail). No transparency. No misleading text (“#1”, “Free money”). |
| **Phone screenshots** | min 2; long side **1080+** | PNG/JPEG | **9:16** or **16:9**. Must depict **real in-app UI**. **ASO Rule:** Use "Hook, Rule, Win" structure. Top 20% of image must be a text-heavy banner with a bold value prop and active verbs (e.g., "SWIPE TO WIN", "COMPETE GLOBALLY"). |
| **Adaptive launcher** | foreground **432×432** | PNG in `mipmap-*` | Must visually match the 512x512 Store Icon to prevent Misleading Claims policy violations. |

### Launcher icon — density table

Generate from one **1024×1024** master (keep safe zone ~66% center for adaptive crop):

| Folder | px |
|--------|-----|
| `mipmap-mdpi` | 48 |
| `mipmap-hdpi` | 72 |
| `mipmap-xhdpi` | 96 |
| `mipmap-xxhdpi` | 144 |
| `mipmap-xxxhdpi` | 192 |

**Adaptive icon:** `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` — separate **background color** (`values/colors.xml`) and **foreground** PNG. Match Balance default: background `#0A0A0A`, foreground = brand mark (e.g. gold cairn / 3×3 grid motif).

### How we generate images & apply icon packages (workflow)

1. **Design brief** — one sentence: subject, background color, flat vs gradient, **no text** on launcher icon unless it exists in-app.
2. **Master art** — Cursor **GenerateImage** or Figma export at 1024×1024 (icon) and 1024×500 (feature graphic).
   - **App Icons (always):** Use [https://easyappicon.com/](https://easyappicon.com/) only — upload square master art → export Play **512×512** + adaptive/mipmap packs. **Never** AppIcon.co, MakeAppIcon, or other icon-pack sites.
   - **Applying Icon Zips via Script:** Use `./scripts/apply-icon-zip.sh "<Game Name>" <zip_or_dir_path>`. The script auto-detects Homebrew OpenJDK 17 (`JAVA_HOME`), unzips/rsyncs launcher mipmaps into `android/app/src/main/res/`, cleans up background XML conflicts, and builds `./gradlew assembleDebug` automatically.
   - **Feature Graphics**: Use [screenshot-maker.appinstitute.com](https://screenshot-maker.appinstitute.com/feature-graphic) or custom SVG Node scripts (`sharp`) to generate exactly 1024×500 Feature Graphics.
   - **SVG & Sharp Generator Safety:** When writing SVG generator scripts with Node + `sharp`, escape all ampersands (`&` → `&amp;` or `and`) and replace unescaped dots (`·` → `-`) to prevent `xmlParseEntityRef` crashes in `librsvg`.
3. **Resize / density export**
   - **Play listing icon:** Export **512×512 32-bit PNG** with alpha — verify with `file play-store-icon-512.png` (must say "PNG image data, 512 x 512, 8-bit/color RGBA"). **Never upload JPEG.**
   - **Android Studio:** Right-click `res` → **New → Image Asset** → Launcher Icons (Adaptive and Legacy) → import master PNG.
   - **CLI (macOS):** `sips -z 512 512 master.png --out play-store-icon-512.png`; loop sizes for mipmaps.
4. **Store screenshots (AAA ASO Framework)** — 9:16 portrait (1080×1920 or 1080×2400). Top 25% = massive bold value proposition header in heavy sans-serif typography; Bottom 75% = 3D device mockup showing active gameplay or product UI:
   - **Screenshot 1 (HOOK):** Core product hook & primary value proposition.
   - **Screenshot 2 (RULE / VERB):** Intuitive core mechanic or primary interaction breakdown.
   - **Screenshot 3 (WIN / REWARD):** Success state, celebration, or primary output display.
   - **Screenshot 4 (MODES / META):** Progression, modes, offline capability, or stats dashboard.
5. **Sanity check** — Side-by-side: **launcher icon ↔ first screen ↔ Play listing icon**. Google **Misleading Claims** rejections often come from icons/screenshots that promise UI the app does not show (wrong colors, fake “Level 100”, unrelated logos on a puzzle game, etc.).

### Play Store listing honesty & ASO checklist

- **ASO Naming Strategy:** Retain descriptive search keywords in the app title (e.g., `BrandName: Descriptive Keyword Subtitle`) to capture organic search volume.
- **Hyper-Literal Icons:** App icons MUST physically depict the core verb or primary interaction on a clean, high-contrast background. Avoid purely abstract logos.
- **Verb-First Descriptions:** Start the listing description with punchy, action-verb bullets rather than generic marketing prose.
- Icon = what users see after install (same palette and motif).
- Screenshots = **default theme** (document which one), not one-off marketing mocks or obsolete UI (e.g. removed “START GAME” splash).
- Short/full description matches **actual** features — level counts from source data (`LEVELS.length`, `levels.json`, etc.), not guesses.
- Feature graphic: app name + real in-app art; avoid stock clip art unrelated to the product.
- **Every bullet** in short + full description must pass the **120-second discoverability test** (§13).
- Standalone Play apps must not borrow parent-portal branding in listing copy (§13).

